  "decisionHub": {
    "whatItIs": "Cisco Webex is an enterprise unified-communications platform spanning meetings, team messaging, whiteboarding, Webex Calling cloud phone, and a separate Webex Contact Center line. A free meetings tier remains published; paid Meet and Suite seats are commonly cited around $12–$14.50 and ~$22.50–$27 per user/month respectively (medium confidence — webex.com/pricing renders dynamically by region/SKU). Enterprise agreements, Calling Professional add-ons, AI Assistant, devices and Contact Center are frequently quote-negotiated inside Cisco EA packaging. Scored as an enterprise UC / Webex Calling peer — not as a thin SMB virtual number and not as a pure CCaaS rank peer to Talkdesk/Genesys/Five9.",
    "bestFor": [
      "Enterprises standardising on Cisco hybrid-work UC (meetings + Calling + messaging)",
      "Organisations already in a Cisco EA that want Calling without a second UCaaS vendor",
      "Buyers who need FedRAMP / regulated meeting paths and room-device ecosystems",
      "mid-market / operations: Cisco Webex fit for mid-market operations teams in the cloud-phone job cluster, from first-party positioning and Business-communications Priority-3 research.",
      "enterprise / operations: Cisco Webex fit for enterprise operations teams in the cloud-phone job cluster, from first-party positioning and Business-communications Priority-3 research."
